<p>For this Service Contract, the following terms shall have the meanings set out below:</p>
<p class="def"><b>“A-Protect”</b> means A-Protect Warranty Corporation, the administrator and service provider of this Service Contract.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Service Contract”</b> or “Contract” means the Terms and Conditions of this Service Contract entered into between the Customer and A-Protect.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“A-Protect Authorized Repair Facility”</b> means a repair facility that has been approved by A-Protect to perform repair or replacement services under this Service Contract.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Alloy Wheels”</b> means road wheels manufactured from a combination of lightweight metals such as aluminum and magnesium, as opposed to wheels made entirely of steel.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Alloy Wheel Repair”</b> means the repair of an Alloy Wheel due to cosmetic damage such as scratches, scuffs, or curb rash.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Commercial/Business Use”</b> means use of the vehicle for purposes other than personal transportation, including but not limited to: taxis, limousines, ride-share or delivery vehicles, courier or rental vehicles, driving school vehicles, vehicles equipped with snowplows, emergency or service vehicles, and vehicles used for racing or competitive driving.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Curb Damage”</b> means cosmetic or structural damage resulting from accidental contact with a curb, including scrapes, scuffs, or curb rash.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Customer”</b> means the registered vehicle owner identified on the front page of this Service Contract, to whom this coverage applies.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Covered Vehicle”</b> means the vehicle identified on the front page of this Service Contract.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Eligible Keys and Remotes”</b> means up to two (2) keys and two (2) remotes originally provided by the selling dealer at the time of vehicle purchase.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Normal Wear and Tear”</b> means the gradual deterioration in operating performance resulting from age, mileage, corrosion, or rust.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Oversized Tires”</b> means any tires with an overall diameter greater than twenty (20) inches.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Paintless Dent Repair”</b> means a non-invasive repair technique used to remove minor dents or dings from a vehicle’s body panels without affecting the original paint finish. The process involves accessing the underside of the panel and using specialized tools to restore the metal to its original shape.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Pre-existing Condition(s)”</b> means any mechanical failure, defect, or operating problem that existed prior to the purchase date.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Road Hazard”</b> means a condition on a public roadway or parking lot that is not normally present, including but not limited to potholes, nails, glass, or other debris.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Selling Dealer”</b> means the authorized dealership or representative through whom the Customer purchased this Service Contract.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Unserviceable”</b> means any tire or wheel that has been punctured, damaged, or otherwise rendered irreparable in A-Protect’s sole discretion, including any alloy wheel that can no longer form an airtight seal with its tire.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Service Contract Coverage Limitations”</b> means the specific exclusions, restrictions, or conditions under which this Service Contract shall become null and void.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Commercial / Business Use”</b> means operation of the Covered Vehicle for purposes other than private passenger transportation, including but not limited to rideshare, delivery, service, courier, sales, or trade use, whether for compensation or incidental to business activity.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Light Commercial Use”</b> means limited business use where the Covered Vehicle is operated primarily for personal transportation and occasionally for commercial purposes (Many small business owners, Uber/Lyft drivers, or realtors drive vehicles), averaging no more than 35,000 kilometres per year.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Medium Commercial Use”</b> means frequent business or delivery use where the Covered Vehicle is operated primarily for commercial purposes, averaging between 35,000 and 60,000 kilometres per year (service vans, couriers, and delivery cars).</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Heavy Commercial Use”</b> means continuous business use, including but not limited to fleet, towing, snowplow, fleet, or other intensive commercial operations exceeding 60,000 kilometres per year.</p>
<p class="def"><b>“Heavy-Duty Vehicle”</b> means a vehicle with a Gross Vehicle Weight Rating (GVWR) greater than 6,350 kilograms (14,000 pounds), or any vehicle used for towing, hauling, or carrying specialized equipment such as snowplows, cargo boxes, or towing apparatus.</p>
<h2 class="part">PART 2: TIRE &amp; RIM PROTECTION PLAN</h2>
<p>The services available under this Service Contract are discretionary service benefits administered by A-Protect and depend on the selections made on the front page of the Application. Coverage applies only to the Registered Vehicle identified on the Application and only during the active Term of this Service Contract. All reimbursements or services are discretionary and are subject to prior authorization by A-Protect, verification of incident details, and submission of valid paid receipts within fourteen (14) days of the occurrence. A-Protect reserves the sole right to inspect the damage, request additional documentation (including photographs or inspection reports), and determine eligibility prior to any approval of reimbursement. Repairs or replacements performed without prior authorization may be denied. Eligibility Requirements: The vehicle must not exceed ten (10) model years prior to the current model year at the time of sale.</p>
<p class="num">2.1 Maximum Liability Limits – This Service Contract shall carry a maximum liability limit which shall not exceed ten thousand dollars ($10,000 CAD) or the verified repair value of the Covered Vehicle, whichever amount is less, at the time of an approved covered repair. The per-claim maximum limit applicable to each individual covered service is outlined in Part 3 of this Service Contract. All reimbursements or approved repairs are subject to prior authorization by A-Protect and are provided at A-Protect’s sole discretion, in accordance with the terms of this Service Contract. Multiple repairs diagnosed at the same time constitute a single claim.</p>

<h2 class="part">PART 3: PARTS &amp; SERVICES COVERED</h2>
<p><b>Protection Plan Selected:</b> Refer to the Application Page for the Protection Plan (Essential, Extended or Superior), term, and any surcharges or add-ons selected.</p>
<p class="lead">*All repairs and reimbursements are at the discretion of A-Protect. The Administrator may select parts that are new, rebuilt, or equivalent quality. All exchanged parts removed by A-Protect or the service centre will remain the property of A-Protect.</p>

<h3 class="ltr">Essential Protection (Section 3.1&#8211;3.3) includes:</h3>
<p class="num"><b>3.1 Tire &amp; Wheel Coverage</b></p>
<p class="num ind"><b>a) Flat Tire Replacement:</b> A-Protect may reimburse the customer up to a maximum of $80 per occurrence for the repair of a flat tire caused by a road hazard, provided the covered vehicle was operated lawfully at the time of the incident.</p>
<p class="num ind"><b>b) Tire Replacement:</b> A-Protect may, at its sole discretion, reimburse the Customer for the reasonable costs to replace up to two (2) tires per occurrence when a Covered Tire becomes Unserviceable as a direct result of a Road Hazard, as defined in this Service Contract. A tire is considered Unserviceable only when it cannot be safely repaired, as determined by A-Protect. Reimbursement may be made up to a maximum of two thousand dollars ($2,000 CAD) for the entire Term of this Service Contract. Replacement tires will be of &#8220;like kind and quality,&#8221; which may include new or used tires and may involve a prorated adjustment based on the remaining tread depth of the damaged tire. If the Covered Vehicle is equipped with factory-installed run-flat tires, the maximum reimbursement limit may increase by up to three thousand dollars ($3,000 CAD) for the Term of this Service Contract, due to the higher cost of run-flat tire replacements. <b>Note: Snow Tires included.</b></p>
<p class="num ind"><b>c) Wheel Replacement:</b> A-Protect may, at its discretion, reimburse the Customer for reasonable costs to repair or replace an Alloy Wheel that has been rendered Unserviceable as a direct result of a Road Hazard, as defined in this Service Contract. Coverage is limited to the replacement of up to two (2) Alloy Wheels per occurrence, with a maximum of four (4) Alloy Wheels during the term of this Service Contract. A-Protect reserves the right to supply or authorize replacement wheels of like kind and quality, which may include new, refurbished, or used components, at A-Protect&#8217;s cost and discretion. Bent Alloy Wheels are eligible for consideration only when the damage was caused by a verified Road Hazard, and the wheel cannot properly seal with its tire as determined by an authorized technician and A-Protect.</p>
<p class="num"><b>3.2 Tire &amp; Wheel Mounting and Balancing</b></p>
<p class="num ind">A-Protect will reimburse the Customer for the reasonable costs for mounting, balancing, valve stems, and tire disposal related to Covered Tire replacements. Unspecified shop fees, environmental charges, and other miscellaneous supplies are excluded.</p>
<p class="num"><b>3.3 Roadside Coverage</b></p>
<p class="num ind">For the Registered Vehicle, A-Protect will reimburse the Customer up to $100 per occurrence for roadside assistance services, limited to: towing (to the nearest A-Protect approved service center), winching, flat tire change (installation of inflated spare; spare not included), fuel delivery (excluding cost of fuel), battery boost, lockout service (excluding locksmith fees). Roadside Assistance is limited to three (3) service calls per twelve (12) month period, and no more than one (1) service call within any twenty-four (24) hour period. Coverage is invalid following Termination of the Service Contract. Valid invoices and proof of payment must be submitted within fourteen (14) days of the occurrence to be eligible for reimbursement.</p>
<p class="num ind">A-Protect does not arrange or dispatch roadside services, reimbursement only.</p>

<h3 class="ltr">Extended Protection (Section 3.1&#8211;3.5) covers all of Essential Protection in addition to:</h3>
<p class="num"><b>3.4 Key Replacement</b></p>
<p class="num ind">In the event the original key (issued at the time of vehicle purchase) is lost, stolen, or destroyed, A-Protect will reimburse up to $800 per Covered Year and shall not exceed $1,600 over the Term of the Service Contract for the reasonable costs to replace a key/remote. Prior authorization from A-Protect is required before any replacement is made. Non-working keys must be available for inspection at A-Protect&#8217;s discretion. The Selling Dealership must provide two (2) keys and two (2) remotes at the time of vehicle delivery.</p>
<p class="num"><b>3.5 Car Rental Coverage</b></p>
<p class="num ind">In the event that a covered repair or replacement under this Service Contract requires more than one (1) business day to complete, A-Protect may, at its discretion, reimburse the Customer up to seventy dollars ($70 CAD) per day for reasonable rental-vehicle expenses. All reimbursements are subject to prior authorization by A-Protect and submission of valid paid receipts within fourteen (14) days of the occurrence.</p>
<p class="num ind">This assistance is administrative in nature and does not constitute insurance coverage or indemnification for loss of use of the vehicle.</p>

<h3 class="ltr">Superior Protection (Section 3.1&#8211;3.5) covers all of Essential and Extended Protection in addition to:</h3>
<p class="num"><b>3.6 Windshield Repair and Replacement</b></p>
<p class="num ind">A&#8209;Protect will reimburse the Customer for the cost of repairs to minor chips and cracks on the vehicle&#8217;s windshield that result directly from damage caused by road hazards, including but not limited to propelled rocks, wood, and metal debris. The maximum reimbursement under this coverage shall be three hundred dollars ($300) per occurrence, not to exceed a total aggregate limit of one thousand dollars ($1,000) over the term of this Service Contract. In the event that a full windshield replacement is required due to such damage, A&#8209;Protect will reimburse the Customer up to one thousand dollars ($1,000) toward the applicable windshield replacement deductible. This replacement coverage is limited to one (1) claim under the term of this Service Contract. Cracks exceeding fifteen (15) centimeters in length are expressly excluded from coverage.</p>
<p class="num"><b>3.7 Headlight, Taillight, Fog Light/Driving Light Lens Repair</b></p>
<p class="num ind">Reimbursement for headlight, taillight, fog light, and driving light lenses for minor chips and cracks only, as a direct result of damage due to road objects, such as propelled rocks or debris (wood, metal pieces/parts), A-Protect will cover up to $150.00 per occurrence or the maximum of $600.00 for the total term of the Service Contract. <b>Exclusions:</b> Cracks over 15 cm are not covered.</p>
<p class="num"><b>3.8 Paintless Dent and Scratch Repair</b></p>
<p class="num ind">A-Protect may, at its discretion, reimburse the Customer for reasonable costs up to two hundred fifty dollars ($250 CAD) per occurrence, to a maximum of one thousand dollars ($1,000 CAD) over the term of this Service Contract. Coverage applies only to minor dents up to five (5) centimetres in diameter or surface scratches up to thirty (30) centimetres in length on external body panels, when the damage is caused directly by public-lot or parking-area incidents, as determined by A&#8209;Protect. Repairs are performed using the Paintless Dent Repair method, where feasible, and are intended to restore the appearance as closely as possible to the original finish. Exact colour or texture matching is not guaranteed. A-Protect reserves the sole right to determine repair eligibility, select the repair facility, and authorize the reimbursement amount.</p>
<p class="num"><b>3.9 Rip/Tear/Burn/Puncture</b></p>
<p class="num ind">For the repair of accidental rips, tears, burns, or punctures up to 3 cm in length for the upholstered seats of the Covered vehicle, A-Protect will cover up to $150.00 per occurrence or the maximum of $600.00 for the total term of the Service Contract.</p>

<h2 class="part">PART 4: CUSTOMER RESPONSIBILITY</h2>
<p class="num">4.1 Regular Vehicle Maintenance – During the Coverage Term of this Service Contract, the Customer shall ensure that all services required to maintain the Covered Vehicle are performed by a licensed repair facility. This includes, but is not limited to, conducting regular tire rotations, maintaining proper inflation levels, and performing timely wheel alignments. The Customer shall also ensure that any mechanical or structural conditions that may affect the performance or integrity of the tires and rims, such as suspension, steering, or wheel balance issues are promptly inspected and repaired when identified. Regular maintenance expenses, including the cost of inspections, adjustments, alignments, balancing, tire rotations, or any other routine services, are expressly excluded from coverage under this Service Contract. Failure to perform, or delay in performing, such maintenance or repairs that results in damage to the tires, rims, or related components shall void coverage for such damage under this Service Contract.</p>
<p class="num">4.2 Vehicle Operation/Safe Driving Practices – The Customer shall operate the Covered Vehicle in a safe, lawful, and prudent manner to prevent avoidable damage to covered components. The Customer shall exercise reasonable care to avoid contact with potholes, curbs, debris, and other road hazards that may cause damage to the tires or rims. Any damage resulting from reckless, negligent, or improper vehicle operation shall not be covered under this Service Contract.</p>
<p class="num">4.3 Claim Reporting &amp; Procedure – The Customer shall comply with the claim procedures set forth under Part 5 of this Service Contract and shall promptly report any damage to the covered tires or rims to A-Protect within a reasonable time following the occurrence. Failure to provide timely notice or to follow the prescribed claim procedures may result in the denial of coverage. A-Protect reserves the right, at its sole discretion, to request photos/videos, or other supporting documentation evidencing the damage at the time of claim submission.</p>

<h2 class="part">PART 5: CLAIMS PROCEDURE</h2>
<p>All claims are subject to prior authorization and documentation review. Unauthorized repairs may be denied.</p>
